From the graph, the curve rises until a local maximum near \(x\approx -2.5\), then falls until a local minimum near \(x\approx 1\), and then rises again.

Thus the function increases where the graph goes upward from left to right, and decreases where it goes downward.

\[
\boxed{
\begin{gathered}
\text{Local maximum at }x\approx -2.5,\qquad
\text{local minimum at }x\approx 1 \;( \text{about }1.1\text{ if read more precisely}).\\[2mm]
\text{Increasing on }(-\infty,-2.5)\cup(1,\infty),\\
\text{Decreasing on }(-2.5,1).
\end{gathered}
}
\]

(Using open intervals; endpoints may be included depending on the convention for increasing/decreasing.)
